# =====================================================================================================================================================================================================
# TILE NAMES AS WRITTEN ON THE BOARD (2026-11-09). The board, the trade screen and the popups show the page.pdl LABEL text (`Coil Plaza`), so a viewer types that, not the id (`Orange3`). The chat resolves a tile by id (unchanged)
# AND by label: longest whole label first, else a unique prefix (first words whole, the last cut), case-insensitive, extra words as before; ambiguous / unknown refused WITH the candidates (id, label, number) and nothing sent.
# The line sent to the engine is the same `prop:<n>` as for the id, so the ledger is the same bytes (proved at the end). Labels are read at parse time from the page.pdl beside the board.pdl in use: nothing is in the C.
# PLACEHOLDER PINS: the 34 rows of `labels_real` pin the 2026-11-09 stand-in names; when the owner's lore names replace the page.pdl rows these expectations are renamed with them (the `labels_fixture` cases do not depend on them).
# =====================================================================================================================================================================================================
CASE    | labels_real
RUN | /usr/bin/grep | -c | Coil Plaza | $T/app/rulesets/classic/page.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | 1 | VACUITY-the-scratch-app-carries-the-placeholder-labels-the-rows-below-pin
RUN | $HOUSE/@.apps/deskopoly/ops/+x/deskopoly_chat.+x | --parse | $T/app | offer p2 give 100 get Coil Plaza
EXPECT_OUT_IS | ok offer p2 give cash:100 get prop:19\nunderstood: offer p2: you give 100 cash, you get Orange3 | THE-HEADLINE-offer-p2-give-100-get-Coil-Plaza-is-Orange3-tile-19
EXPECT_EXIT | 0 | headline-exit-0
RUN | $HOUSE/@.apps/deskopoly/ops/+x/deskopoly_chat.+x | --parse | $T/app | offer p2 give 100 get Orange3
EXPECT_OUT_IS | ok offer p2 give cash:100 get prop:19\nunderstood: offer p2: you give 100 cash, you get Orange3 | the-id-form-gives-the-very-same-canonical-line
